<H4 class=3DH3><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Gathering=20
System Statistics</FONT></H4><!--/TOC=3Dh3--><A name=3D28811></A>
<P class=3DBP>System statistics enable the optimizer to consider a =
system's I/O=20
and CPU performance and utilization. For each plan candidate, the =
optimizer=20
computes estimates for I/O and CPU costs. It is important to know the =
system=20
characteristics to pick the most efficient plan with optimal proportion =
between=20
I/O and CPU cost.</P><A name=3D28812></A>
<P class=3DBP>System I/O characteristics depend on many factors and do =
not stay=20
constant all the time. Using system statistics management routines, =
database=20
administrators can capture statistics in the interval of time when the =
system=20
has the most common workload. For example, database applications can =
process=20
OLTP transactions during the day and run OLAP reports at night. =
Administrators=20
can gather statistics for both states and activate appropriate OLTP or =
OLAP=20
statistics when needed. This enables the optimizer to generate relevant =
costs=20
with respect to available system resource plans.</P><A name=3D28813></A>
<P class=3DBP>When Oracle generates system statistics, it analyzes =
system activity=20
in a specified period of time. Unlike table, index, or column =
statistics, Oracle=20
does not invalidate already parsed SQL statements when system statistics =
get=20
updated. All new SQL statements are parsed using new statistics. Oracle=20
Corporation highly recommends that you gather system statistics.</P><A=20
name=3D28814></A>
<P class=3DBP>The =
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>GATHER_SYSTEM_STATS</CODE> routine=20
collects system statistics in a user-defined timeframe. You can also set =
system=20
statistics values explicitly using=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>SET_SYSTEM_STATS</CODE>. Use=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>GET_SYSTEM_STATS</CODE> to verify system=20
statistics.</P><A name=3D28819></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNote dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to format =
a note"=20
cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
summary=3D"This is a layout table to format a note" border=3D0>
  <TBODY>
  <TR class=3DNote>
    <TD class=3DNote>
      <HR>
      <A name=3D28817></A><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, =
sans-serif"><STRONG=20
      class=3DNH>Note:</STRONG></FONT> <A name=3D28818></A>
      <P class=3DNB>You must have DBA privileges to update dictionary =
system=20
      statistics.</P>
      <HR>
    </TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A name=3D33255></A>
<P class=3DBP><A=20
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/stats.htm#33258">Example&nbsp;3-1</A>=20
shows database applications processing OLTP transactions during the day =
and=20
running reports at night. First, system statistics must be collected. =
The values=20
in this example are user-defined; in other words, you must determine an=20
appropriate time interval and name for your environment.</P><A =
name=3D33258></A>
<H4 class=3DET><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><EM>Example =
3-1=20
Generating System Statistics</EM></FONT></H4><A name=3D33259></A>
<P class=3DBP>Gather statistics during the day. Gathering ends after 720 =
minutes=20
and is stored in the <CODE>mystats</CODE> table:</P><PRE class=3DCE><A =
name=3D29363></A>BEGIN
<A name=3D34720></A>DBMS_STATS.GATHER_SYSTEM_STATS(
<A name=3D34721></A>             gathering_mode =3D&gt; 'interval',
<A name=3D34722></A>             interval =3D&gt; 720,
<A name=3D28825></A>             stattab =3D&gt; 'mystats',
<A name=3D28826></A>             statid =3D&gt; 'OLTP');
<A name=3D28827></A>END;
<A name=3D28828></A>/
<A name=3D28829></A>
</PRE><A name=3D28830></A>
<P class=3DBP>Gather statistics during the night. Gathering ends after =
720 minutes=20
and is stored in the <CODE>mystats</CODE> table:</P><PRE class=3DCE><A =
name=3D28831></A>BEGIN
<A name=3D34733></A>DBMS_STATS.GATHER_SYSTEM_STATS(
<A name=3D34734></A>             gathering_mode =3D&gt; 'interval',
<A name=3D34735></A>             interval =3D&gt; 720,
<A name=3D34736></A>             stattab =3D&gt; 'mystats',
<A name=3D34737></A>             statid =3D&gt; 'OLAP');
<A name=3D28835></A>END;
<A name=3D28836></A>/
<A name=3D28837></A>
</PRE><A name=3D28838></A>
<P class=3DBP>If appropriate, you can switch between the statistics =
gathered. It=20
is possible to automate this process by submitting a job to update the=20
dictionary with appropriate statistics.</P><A name=3D29615></A>
<P class=3DBP>During the day, the following jobs import the OLTP =
statistics for=20
the daytime run:</P><PRE class=3DCE><A name=3D28839></A>VARIABLE jobno =
number;
<A name=3D28840></A>BEGIN
<A name=3D28841></A>   DBMS_JOB.SUBMIT(:jobno,
<A name=3D28842></A>      =
'DBMS_STATS.IMPORT_SYSTEM_STATS(''mystats'',''OLTP'');'
<A name=3D28843></A>      SYSDATE, 'SYSDATE + 1');
<A name=3D28844></A>   COMMIT;
<A name=3D28845></A>END;
<A name=3D28846></A>/
<A name=3D28847></A>
</PRE><A name=3D29391></A>
<P class=3DBP>During the night, the following jobs import the OLAP =
statistics for=20
the nighttime run:</P><PRE class=3DCE><A name=3D29389></A>BEGIN
<A name=3D28848></A>   DBMS_JOB.SUBMIT(:jobno,
<A name=3D28849></A>      =
'DBMS_STATS.IMPORT_SYSTEM_STATS(''mystats'',''OLAP'');'
<A name=3D28850></A>      SYSDATE + 0.5, 'SYSDATE + 1');
<A name=3D28851></A>   COMMIT;
<A name=3D28852></A>END;
<A name=3D28853></A>/
</PRE><A name=3D28863></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNoteAlso dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to =
format a note"=20
cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
