href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/appdev.920/a966=
12/d_stats.htm#ARPLS059"><EM=20
      class=3DItalic>Oracle9i Supplied PL/SQL Packages and Types=20
      Reference</EM></A> for detailed information on the procedures in =
the=20
      <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE> package for implementing system=20
  statistics</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A =
name=3D28808></A><!--TOC=3Dh3-"28808"-->
<H4 class=3DH3><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Gathering=20
Index Statistics</FONT></H4><!--/TOC=3Dh3--><A name=3D26597></A>
<P class=3DBP>Oracle can gather some statistics automatically while =
creating or=20
rebuilding a B-tree or bitmap index. The <CODE>COMPUTE</CODE>=20
<CODE>STATISTICS</CODE> option of <CODE>CREATE</CODE> <CODE>INDEX</CODE> =
or=20
<CODE>ALTER</CODE> <CODE>INDEX</CODE> ... <CODE>REBUILD</CODE> enables =
this=20
gathering of statistics.</P><A name=3D26598></A>
<P class=3DBP>The statistics that Oracle gathers for the =
<CODE>COMPUTE</CODE>=20
<CODE>STATISTICS</CODE> option depend on whether the index is =
partitioned or=20
nonpartitioned.</P>
<UL class=3DLB1>
  <LI class=3DLB1 type=3Ddisc><A name=3D26599></A>For a nonpartitioned =
index, Oracle=20
  gathers index, table, and column statistics while creating or =
rebuilding the=20
  index. In a concatenated-key index, the column statistics refer only =
to the=20
  leading column of the key.=20
  <LI class=3DLB1 type=3Ddisc><A name=3D26600></A>For a partitioned =
index, Oracle does=20
  not gather any table or column statistics while creating the index or=20
  rebuilding its partitions.=20
  <UL class=3DLD2>
    <LI class=3DLD2 type=3DCIRCLE><A name=3D26601></A>While creating a =
partitioned=20
    index, Oracle gathers index statistics for each partition and for =
the entire=20
    index. If the index uses composite partitioning, then Oracle also =
gathers=20
    statistics for each subpartition.=20
    <LI class=3DLD2 type=3DCIRCLE><A name=3D26602></A>While rebuilding a =
partition or=20
    subpartition of an index, Oracle gathers index statistics only for =
that=20
    partition or subpartition. </LI></UL></LI></UL><A name=3D26603></A>
<P class=3DBP>To ensure correctness of the statistics, Oracle always =
uses base=20
tables when creating an index with the <CODE>COMPUTE</CODE>=20
<CODE>STATISTICS</CODE> option, even if another index is available that =
could be=20
used to create the index.</P><A name=3D26593></A>
<P class=3DBP>If you do not use the <CODE>COMPUTE</CODE> =
<CODE>STATISTICS</CODE>=20
clause, or if you have made significant changes to the data, then use =
the=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>GATHER_INDEX_STATS</CODE> procedure to =
collect=20
index statistics.</P><A name=3D25701></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNoteAlso dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to =
format a note"=20
