40/toc.htm">Oracle9i=20
      SQL Reference</A></EM> for more information about the =
<CODE>COMPUTE</CODE>=20
      <CODE>STATISTICS</CODE> =
clause</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A=20
name=3D33195></A><!--TOC=3Dh4-"33195"-->
<H5 class=3DH4><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Gathering=20
Statistics for Function-Based Indexes</FONT></H5><!--/TOC=3Dh4--><A=20
name=3D33131></A>
<P class=3DBP>You should analyze the table after creating a =
function-based index,=20
to allow Oracle to collect column statistics equivalent information for =
the=20
expression. Optionally, you can collect histograms for the index =
expressions by=20
specifying <CODE>for</CODE> <CODE>all</CODE> <CODE>hidden</CODE>=20
<CODE>columns</CODE> <CODE>size</CODE> =
<EM><CODE>number_of_buckets</CODE></EM>=20
in the <CODE>METHOD_OPT</CODE> argument to the <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>=20
procedures.</P><A name=3D33284></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNoteAlso dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to =
format a note"=20
cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
summary=3D"This is a layout table to format a note" border=3D0>
  <TBODY>
  <TR class=3DNoteAlso>
    <TD class=3DNoteAlso><A name=3D33290></A><FONT=20
      face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><STRONG class=3DNH>See=20
      Also:</STRONG></FONT> <A name=3D33291></A>
      <UL class=3DNL>
        <LI class=3DNL type=3Ddisc><A name=3D33376></A><A=20
        =
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/stats.htm#27124">"Using=20
        Histograms"</A><A=20
        =
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/stats.htm#27124"></A>=20

        <LI class=3DNL type=3Ddisc><A name=3D33380></A><EM =
