syntax of=20
        the <CODE>METHOD_OPT</CODE> argument=20
</LI></UL></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A =
name=3D33117></A><!--TOC=3Dh3-"33117"-->
<H4 class=3DH3><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Gathering=20
New Optimizer Statistics</FONT></H4><!--/TOC=3Dh3--><A name=3D25704></A>
<P class=3DBP>Before gathering new statistics for a particular schema, =
use the=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>EXPORT_SCHEMA_STATS</CODE> procedure to =
extract=20
and save existing statistics. Then use=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>GATHER_SCHEMA_STATS</CODE> to gather new=20
statistics. You can implement both of these with a single call to the=20
<CODE>GATHER_SCHEMA_STATS</CODE> procedure, by specifying additional=20
parameters.</P><A name=3D29401></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNoteAlso dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to =
format a note"=20
cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
summary=3D"This is a layout table to format a note" border=3D0>
  <TBODY>
  <TR class=3DNoteAlso>
    <TD class=3DNoteAlso><A name=3D29404></A><FONT=20
      face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><STRONG class=3DNH>See=20
      Also:</STRONG></FONT> <A name=3D29405></A>
      <P class=3DNB><A=20
      =
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/stats.htm#25787">"Preserving=20
      Versions of Statistics"</A><A=20
      =
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/stats.htm#25787"></A></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A=20
name=3D25705></A>
<P class=3DBP>If key SQL statements experience significant performance=20
degradation, then you can either gather statistics again using a larger =
sample=20
size or perform the following steps:</P>
<OL class=3DLN1 type=3D1>
  <LI class=3DLN1 type=3D1 value=3D1><A name=3D27955></A>Use=20
  <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>EXPORT_SCHEMA_STATS</CODE> to save the =
new=20
  statistics in a different statistics table or a statistics table with =
a=20
  different statistics identifier.=20
  <LI class=3DLN1 type=3D1 value=3D2><A name=3D25707></A>Use=20
  <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>IMPORT_SCHEMA_STATS</CODE> to restore =
the old=20
  statistics. The application is now ready to run again. </LI></OL><A=20
name=3D25708></A>
<P class=3DBP>You might want to use the new statistics if they result in =
improved=20
performance for the majority of SQL statements and if the number of =
problem SQL=20
statements is small. In this case, perform the following steps:</P>
<OL class=3DLN1 type=3D1>
  <LI class=3DLN1 type=3D1 value=3D1><A name=3D25709></A>Create a stored =
outline for=20
  each problematic SQL statement, using the old statistics. Stored =
outlines are=20
  precompiled execution plans that Oracle can use to mimic proven =
application=20
  performance characteristics.=20
  <P><A name=3D25714></A></P>
  <DIV align=3Dcenter>
  <TABLE class=3DNoteAlso dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to =
format a note"=20
  cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
