    <TBODY>
    <TR class=3DNoteAlso>
      <TD class=3DNoteAlso><A name=3D25712></A><FONT=20
        face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><STRONG class=3DNH><STRONG =

        class=3DBold>See Also</STRONG>:</STRONG></FONT> <A =
name=3D25713></A>
        <P class=3DNB><A=20
        =
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/outlines.htm#13547">Chapter&nbsp;7,=20
        "Using Plan Stability"</A></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV>
  <LI class=3DLN1 type=3D1 value=3D2><A name=3D25716></A>Use=20
  <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>IMPORT_SCHEMA_STATS</CODE> to restore =
the new=20
  statistics. The application is now ready to run with the new =
statistics.=20
  However, you will continue to achieve the previous performance levels =
for the=20
  problem SQL statements. </LI></OL><A =
name=3D25727></A><!--TOC=3Dh3-"25727"-->
<H4 class=3DH3><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Gathering=20
Automated Statistics</FONT></H4><!--/TOC=3Dh3--><A name=3D25728></A>
<P class=3DBP>You can automatically gather statistics or create lists of =
tables=20
that have stale or no statistics. To automatically gather statistics, =
run the=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>GATHER_SCHEMA_STATS</CODE> and=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>GATHER_DATABASE_STATS</CODE> procedures =
with the=20
<CODE>OPTIONS</CODE> and <CODE>objlist</CODE> parameters. Use the values =
listed=20
in <A=20
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
33/stats.htm#36292">Table&nbsp;3-2</A>=20
for the <CODE>options</CODE> parameter.</P>
<H5 class=3DTT><A name=3D36289></A><A name=3D36292></A><STRONG><FONT=20
face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><EM>Table 3-2 Options Parameters =
for=20
Gathering Statistics</EM></FONT></STRONG></H5>
<TABLE class=3DFormal dir=3Dltr title=3D"" cellSpacing=3D0 =
cellPadding=3D3 rules=3Dgroups=20
width=3D"100%" summary=3D"" border=3D1 frame=3Dhsides>
  <THEAD>
  <TR class=3DFormal>
    <TH class=3DFormal vAlign=3Dbottom scope=3Dcol align=3Dleft><A=20
      name=3D36296></A><FONT=20
      face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, =
sans-serif"><STRONG>Value</STRONG></FONT></TH>
    <TH class=3DFormal vAlign=3Dbottom scope=3Dcol align=3Dleft><A=20
      name=3D36298></A><FONT=20
      face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, =
sans-serif"><STRONG>Meaning</STRONG></FONT></TH></TR></THEAD>
  <TBODY>
  <TR class=3DFormal vAlign=3Dtop align=3Dleft>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36336></A>
      <P class=3DTB><CODE>GATHER STALE</CODE></P></TD>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36338></A>
      <P class=3DTB>Gathers statistics on tables with stale =
statistics.</P></TD></TR>
  <TR class=3DFormal vAlign=3Dtop align=3Dleft>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36332></A>
      <P class=3DTB><CODE>GATHER</CODE></P></TD>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36334></A>
      <P class=3DTB>Gathers statistics on all tables. =
(default)</P></TD></TR>
  <TR class=3DFormal vAlign=3Dtop align=3Dleft>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36328></A>
      <P class=3DTB><CODE>GATHER EMPTY</CODE></P></TD>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36330></A>
      <P class=3DTB>Gathers statistics only on tables without=20
statistics.</P></TD></TR>
  <TR class=3DFormal vAlign=3Dtop align=3Dleft>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36324></A>
      <P class=3DTB><CODE>LIST STALE</CODE></P></TD>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36326></A>
      <P class=3DTB>Creates a list of tables with stale =
statistics.</P></TD></TR>
  <TR class=3DFormal vAlign=3Dtop align=3Dleft>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36320></A>
      <P class=3DTB><CODE>LIST EMPTY</CODE></P></TD>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36322></A>
      <P class=3DTB>Creates a list of tables that do not have=20
statistics.</P></TD></TR>
  <TR class=3DFormal vAlign=3Dtop align=3Dleft>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36316></A>
      <P class=3DTB><CODE>GATHER AUTO</CODE></P></TD>
    <TD class=3DFormal><A name=3D36318></A>
      <P class=3DTB>Gathers <EM class=3DItalic>all</EM> the statistics =
for the=20
      objects of a specific schema (or database with=20
      <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>GATHER_DATABASE_STATS()</CODE>) that =
are not=20
      up-to-date.</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE><A name=3D30936></A>
<P class=3DBP>The <CODE>objlist</CODE> parameter identifies an output =
parameter=20
for the <CODE>LIST</CODE> <CODE>STALE</CODE> and <CODE>LIST</CODE>=20
<CODE>EMPTY</CODE> options. The <CODE>objlist</CODE> parameter is of =
type=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>OBJECTTAB</CODE>.</P><A =
name=3D25754></A><!--TOC=3Dh4-"25754"-->
<H5 class=3DH4><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Designating=20
Tables for Monitoring and Automated Statistics =
Gathering</FONT></H5><!--/TOC=3Dh4--><A name=3D29157></A>
<P class=3DBP>Before you can utilize automated statistics gathering for =
a=20
particular table, you must bring either the tables of a specific schema =
or a=20
complete database into the monitoring mode. Do this with the=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>ALTER_SCHEMA_TAB_MONITORING</CODE> or=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>ALTER_DATABASE_TAB_MONITORING</CODE> =
procedures.=20
Alternatively, you can enable the monitoring attribute using the=20
<CODE>MONITORING</CODE> keyword. This keyword is part of the =
<CODE>CREATE</CODE>=20
<CODE>TABLE</CODE> and <CODE>ALTER</CODE> <CODE>TABLE</CODE> statement =
syntax.=20
Monitoring tracks the approximate number of <CODE>INSERT</CODE>s,=20
<CODE>UPDATE</CODE>s, and <CODE>DELETE</CODE>s for that table since the =
last=20
time statistics were gathered. Oracle uses this data to identify tables =
with=20
stale statistics. Then, you can enable automated statistics gathering by =
setting=20
up a recurring job (perhaps by using job queues) that invokes=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>GATHER_TABLE_STATS</CODE> with the=20
<CODE>GATHER</CODE> <CODE>STALE</CODE> option at an appropriate interval =
for=20
your application.</P><A name=3D29163></A>
<P class=3DBP>Objects are considered stale when 10% of the total rows =
have been=20
changed. When you issue <CODE>GATHER_TABLE_STATS</CODE> with =
<CODE>GATHER</CODE>=20
<CODE>STALE</CODE>, the procedure checks the =
<CODE>USER_TAB_MODIFICATIONS</CODE>=20
view. If a monitored table has been modified more than 10%, then =
statistics are=20
gathered again. The information about changes of tables, as shown in the =

<CODE>USER_TAB_MODIFICATIONS</CODE> view, can be flushed from the SGA =
into the=20
data dictionary with the=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>FLUSH_DATABASE_MONITORING_INFO</CODE>=20
procedure.</P><A name=3D25762></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNote dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to format =
a note"=20
cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
summary=3D"This is a layout table to format a note" border=3D0>
  <TBODY>
  <TR class=3DNote>
    <TD class=3DNote>
      <HR>
      <A name=3D25760></A><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, =
sans-serif"><STRONG=20
      class=3DNH><STRONG class=3DBold>Note</STRONG>:</STRONG></FONT> <A=20
      name=3D25761></A>
      <P class=3DNB>There can be a few minutes delay while Oracle =
propagates=20
      information to this view.</P>
      <HR>
    </TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A name=3D25763></A>
<P class=3DBP>To disable monitoring, use the=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>ALTER_SCHEMA_TAB_MONITORING</CODE> or=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>.<CODE>ALTER_DATABASE_TAB_MONITORING</CODE> =
procedures,=20
or use the <CODE>NOMONITORING</CODE> keyword.</P><A name=3D25773></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNoteAlso dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to =
format a note"=20
cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
summary=3D"This is a layout table to format a note" border=3D0>
  <TBODY>
  <TR class=3DNoteAlso>
    <TD class=3DNoteAlso><A name=3D25766></A><FONT=20
      face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><STRONG class=3DNH>See=20
      Also:</STRONG></FONT> <A name=3D25767></A>
      <P class=3DNB><EM class=3DItalic><A class=3D"olinkSRC SQLRF"=20
      =
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/server.920/a965=
40/toc.htm">Oracle9i=20
      SQL Reference</A></EM> for more information about the =
<CODE>CREATE</CODE>=20
      <CODE>TABLE</CODE> and <CODE>ALTER</CODE> <CODE>TABLE</CODE> =
syntax and=20
      the <CODE>MONITORING</CODE> and <CODE>NOMONITORING</CODE>=20
  keywords</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A =
name=3D25774></A><!--TOC=3Dh4-"25774"-->
<H5 class=3DH4><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Enabling=20
Automated Statistics Gathering</FONT></H5><!--/TOC=3Dh4--><A =
name=3D25775></A>
<P class=3DBP>The <CODE>GATHER</CODE> <CODE>STALE</CODE> option gathers =
statistics=20
only for tables that have stale statistics and for which you have =
enabled=20
monitoring.</P><A name=3D27965></A>
<P class=3DBP>The <CODE>GATHER</CODE> <CODE>STALE</CODE> option =
maintains=20
up-to-date statistics for the cost-based optimizer. Using this option at =
regular=20
intervals also avoids the overhead associated with gathering statistics =
on all=20
tables at one time. The <CODE>GATHER</CODE> option can incur much more =
overhead,=20
because this option generally gathers statistics for a greater number of =
tables=20
than <CODE>GATHER</CODE> <CODE>STALE</CODE>.</P><A name=3D25783></A>
<P class=3DBP>Use a script or job scheduling tool for the=20
<CODE>GATHER_SCHEMA_STATS</CODE> and <CODE>GATHER_DATABASE_STATS</CODE>=20
procedures to establish a frequency of statistics collection that is =
appropriate=20
for the application. The frequency of collection intervals should =
balance the=20
task of providing accurate statistics for the optimizer against the =
processing=20
overhead incurred by the statistics collection process.</P><A =
name=3D25784></A><!--TOC=3Dh4-"25784"-->
<H5 class=3DH4><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Creating=20
Lists of Tables with Stale or No =
Statistics</FONT></H5><!--/TOC=3Dh4--><A=20
name=3D25785></A>
<P class=3DBP>You can use the <CODE>GATHER_SCHEMA_STATS</CODE> and=20
<CODE>GATHER_DATABASE_STATS</CODE> procedures to create a list of tables =
with=20
stale statistics. You can also use these procedures to create a list of =
tables=20
with no statistics. Use the lists to identify tables for which you want =
to=20
gather manual statistics.</P><A name=3D25787></A><!--TOC=3Dh3-"25787"-->
<H4 class=3DH3><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Preserving=20
Versions of Statistics</FONT></H4><!--/TOC=3Dh3--><A name=3D25788></A>
<P class=3DBP>You can preserve versions of statistics for tables by =
specifying the=20
<CODE>stattab</CODE>, <CODE>statid</CODE>, and <CODE>statown</CODE> =
parameters=20
in the <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE> package. Use <CODE>stattab</CODE> to =
identify a=20
destination table for archiving previous versions of statistics. Further =

identify these versions using <CODE>statid</CODE> to denote the date and =
time=20
the version was made. Use <CODE>statown</CODE> to identify a destination =
schema,=20
if it is different from the schema(s) of the actual tables. You must =
first=20
create such a table, using the <CODE>CREATE_STAT_TABLE</CODE> procedure =
of the=20
<CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE> package.</P><A name=3D25800></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNoteAlso dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to =
format a note"=20
cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
summary=3D"This is a layout table to format a note" border=3D0>
