information=20
      on <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE> procedures and=20
parameters</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A =
name=3D29318></A><!--TOC=3Dh2-"29318"-->
<H3 class=3DH2><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Using the=20
ANALYZE Statement</FONT></H3><!--/TOC=3Dh2--><A name=3D34424></A>
<P class=3DBP>You can use the ANALYZE statement to generate statistics =
for=20
cost-based optimization.</P><A name=3D36029></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNote dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to format =
a note"=20
cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 width=3D"80%"=20
summary=3D"This is a layout table to format a note" border=3D0>
  <TBODY>
  <TR class=3DNote>
    <TD class=3DNote>
      <HR>
      <A name=3D36019></A><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, =
sans-serif"><STRONG=20
      class=3DNH>Note:</STRONG></FONT> <A name=3D36020></A>
      <P class=3DNB>Oracle Corporation strongly recommends that you use =
the=20
      <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE> package rather than <CODE>ANALYZE</CODE> =
to=20
      collect optimizer statistics. That package lets you collect =
statistics in=20
      parallel, collect global statistics for partitioned objects, and =
fine tune=20
      your statistics collection in other ways. Further, the cost-based=20
      optimizer will eventually use only statistics that have been =
collected by=20
      <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE>. See <EM class=3DItalic><A =
class=3D"olinkSRC ARPLS"=20
      =
href=3D"http://www.cise.ufl.edu/help/database/oracle-docs/appdev.920/a966=
12/toc.htm">Oracle9i=20
      Supplied PL/SQL Packages and Types Reference</A></EM> for more =
information=20
      on this package. <A name=3D36026></A></P>
      <P class=3DNB>However, you must use the <CODE>ANALYZE</CODE> =
statement=20
      rather than <CODE>DBMS_STATS</CODE> for statistics collection not =
related=20
      to the cost-based optimizer, such as:</P>
      <UL class=3DNL>
        <LI class=3DNL type=3Ddisc><A name=3D36027></A>To use the=20
        <CODE>VALIDATE</CODE> or <CODE>LIST CHAINED ROWS</CODE> clauses=20
        <LI class=3DNL type=3Ddisc><A name=3D36028></A>To collect =
information on=20
        freelist blocks </LI></UL>
      <HR>
    </TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV><A =
name=3D29436></A><!--TOC=3Dh2-"29436"-->
<H3 class=3DH2><FONT face=3D"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" =
color=3D#330099>Finding=20
Data Distribution</FONT></H3><!--/TOC=3Dh2--><A name=3D25907></A>
<P class=3DBP>The statistics gathered help you determine how the data is =

distributed across the tables. The optimizer assumes that the data is =
uniformly=20
distributed. You can analyze the actual data distribution in the tables =
by=20
viewing the appropriate dictionary table: <CODE>DBA_TABLES</CODE> for =
tables and=20
<CODE>DBA_TAB_COL_STATISTICS</CODE> for column statistics.</P><A =
name=3D25908></A>
<P class=3DBP>You can use histograms to determine attribute skew.</P><A=20
name=3D26954></A>
<DIV align=3Dcenter>
<TABLE class=3DNoteAlso dir=3Dltr title=3D"This is a layout table to =
format a note"=20
